{
  "moduleId": "m00224",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00224:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Conjugate Addition of Amines"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "ef872dd5-bdb0-484f-8ead-117a80ef8c90"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00224:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00224:caption:fig-00001-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00224:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "In direct (1,2) addition, nucleophile attacks carbonyl, forms alcohol after protonation. In conjugate (1,4) addition, nucleophile attacks beta carbon of alpha-beta unsaturated aldehyde or ketone to form saturated after protonation."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_19_13_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00224:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00224:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "The ball-and-stick model in electrostatic potential map of an alpha-beta-unsaturated aldehyde or ketone. Resonance structures with negative on oxygen and positive on carbonyl and beta carbon are shown."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_19_13_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00224:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00224:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "Double bond of alpha-beta unsaturated ketone or aldehyde is activated, susceptible to nucleophilic attack. Double bond with no adjacent carbonyl is unactivated, not susceptible to nucleophilic attack."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_19_13_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00224:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "Conjugate Addition of Amines"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00004",
          "segmentId": "m00224:para:para-00004"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00004",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00224:alt:fig-00004-alt",
              "text": "2-Cyclohexenone undergoes reversible reactions with methylamine to form beta-amino ketone (sole product). A second pathway shows intermediate ion leading to an unsaturated imine that is not formed."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_13_004.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00002",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00224:title:sect-00002-title",
        "text": "Conjugate Addition of Water"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00005",
          "segmentId": "m00224:para:para-00005"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00005",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00224:alt:fig-00005-alt",
              "text": "Cis-aconitate ([1Z]-prop-1-ene-1,2,3-tricarboxyate) reacts with water to form isocitrate ([1R,2S]-1-hydroxypropane-1,2,3-tricarboxylic acid)."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_19_13_005.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00003",
      "class": "section-exercises",
